1
00:01:47,370 --> 00:02:08,480
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:08,720 --> 00:02:10,690
Listen to me carefully, Osman Bey.

3
00:02:11,880 --> 00:02:13,630
Be my banner lord.

4
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:15,490
Shake the world.

5
00:02:23,730 --> 00:02:26,320
You're looking for a dog like Alişar...

6
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:32,800
not a banner lord.

7
00:02:34,830 --> 00:02:37,690
Balgay says a thing for just once.

8
00:02:37,740 --> 00:02:41,420
And when he says that, he
shakes the world.

9
00:02:41,870 --> 00:02:44,560
Mountains surrender.

10
00:02:44,770 --> 00:02:48,770
Don't you know that we've
opposed to many rulers?

11
00:02:50,810 --> 00:02:56,130
I say that I want every piece
of land including seas.

12
00:02:57,520 --> 00:03:01,520
Every castle, every city and...

13
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:04,340
Constantine.

14
00:03:08,400 --> 00:03:11,340
Your desires blind many people.

15
00:03:12,930 --> 00:03:14,420
But...

16
00:03:15,310 --> 00:03:22,010
I'll teach you that the blood in my
veins won't bow down to anyone.

17
00:03:25,250 --> 00:03:26,990
How dare you?

18
00:03:27,920 --> 00:03:32,590
How do you think you can order me?

19
00:03:34,940 --> 00:03:38,620
Obey me, Osman.

20
00:03:38,970 --> 00:03:42,970
Obey me so that your Alps...

21
00:03:43,450 --> 00:03:45,600
will batten the smell of blood.

22
00:03:46,290 --> 00:03:48,380
The day I obey you...

23
00:03:49,350 --> 00:03:51,860
will become the day that
Turk's traditions die.

24
00:03:56,310 --> 00:04:00,850
I disregard your traditions.

25
00:04:00,850 --> 00:04:03,150
And I make rugs from corpses...

26
00:04:03,150 --> 00:04:06,100
like you.

27
00:04:21,670 --> 00:04:23,320
Obey...

28
00:04:23,920 --> 00:04:25,560
or die.

29
00:04:30,080 --> 00:04:35,120
Shahada or freedom.

30
00:05:01,640 --> 00:05:04,370
Tell your soldiers to bring us water.

31
00:05:05,040 --> 00:05:07,980
We dried up because we
killed so many of you.

32
00:05:09,070 --> 00:05:12,090
You'll lick the mud on my shoes, Turk.

33
00:05:12,620 --> 00:05:14,520
It'll be enough for you.

34
00:05:17,640 --> 00:05:21,640
Will you be able to say that
when I'm killing you?

35
00:05:50,920 --> 00:05:52,160
Dündar Bey.

36
00:05:52,650 --> 00:05:53,940
My Gündüz.

37
00:06:12,610 --> 00:06:15,810
Uncle! Uncle! Uncle!

38
00:06:17,660 --> 00:06:20,080
Dündar Bey!

39
00:06:33,220 --> 00:06:34,540
Bamsı Bey.

40
00:06:38,080 --> 00:06:40,940
- Where's Osman?
- How's Osman?

41
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:45,160
He's talking to Balgay. Balgay
wants something from him.

42
00:06:55,760 --> 00:06:59,760
I don't know how to live
with this black destiny.

43
00:07:00,710 --> 00:07:02,700
Shuu up and walk.

44
00:07:07,890 --> 00:07:09,230
Walk!

45
00:07:48,790 --> 00:07:50,350
Be ready.

46
00:07:51,070 --> 00:07:52,390
We'll kill them...

47
00:07:52,390 --> 00:07:56,430
with our weapons.

48
00:07:58,540 --> 00:08:01,400
We'll go with Osman if necessary.

49
00:08:01,880 --> 00:08:04,710
- Be ready.
- Thanks, my Bey.

50
00:08:09,830 --> 00:08:11,820
Wait here.

51
00:08:19,840 --> 00:08:26,250
Die with your Alps or
glorify your soul.

52
00:08:29,050 --> 00:08:30,880
Your decision.

53
00:08:38,340 --> 00:08:39,690
Commander Balgay.

54
00:08:39,840 --> 00:08:42,170
The tents know about you.

55
00:08:42,630 --> 00:08:45,880
Everyone felt Balgay's power.

56
00:08:47,640 --> 00:08:52,590
Go to New Bazaar and...

57
00:08:53,330 --> 00:08:56,640
bring Sheikh Edebalı to me.

58
00:08:57,310 --> 00:09:01,680
Dervishes will be in New Bazaar.

59
00:10:03,630 --> 00:10:05,710
I wanted you to eat something.

60
00:10:07,040 --> 00:10:08,920
And I brought you water.

61
00:10:15,620 --> 00:10:16,700
My Sheikh.

62
00:10:19,110 --> 00:10:21,950
I want to say something if you let me.

63
00:10:29,640 --> 00:10:31,420
I'm guilty.

64
00:10:32,910 --> 00:10:34,760
I went too far.

65
00:10:34,990 --> 00:10:36,520
I didn't listen to you.

66
00:10:37,400 --> 00:10:40,050
I knew but I was late.

67
00:10:44,410 --> 00:10:46,520
Forgive me.

68
00:10:50,830 --> 00:10:53,700
Where is the difference...

69
00:10:55,350 --> 00:10:56,970
between the devil and human, Bala?

70
00:11:00,640 --> 00:11:02,210
Allah created the devil...

71
00:11:03,120 --> 00:11:08,160
to obey Adam.

72
00:11:08,900 --> 00:11:10,450
The devil didn't listen to him.

73
00:11:11,590 --> 00:11:13,660
He sinned.

74
00:11:14,240 --> 00:11:16,170
Allah...

75
00:11:17,330 --> 00:11:22,220
wanted Adam to stay away from
the forbidden fruit.

76
00:11:23,540 --> 00:11:25,990
Adam didn't listen to him.

77
00:11:27,140 --> 00:11:29,200
He sinned.

78
00:11:34,180 --> 00:11:36,020
Both of them...

79
00:11:37,560 --> 00:11:39,950
didn't listen.

80
00:11:40,710 --> 00:11:45,670
The devil was so arrogant but...

81
00:11:46,520 --> 00:11:49,940
Adam swore off.

82
00:11:50,690 --> 00:11:52,380
He apologized.

83
00:11:52,750 --> 00:11:56,750
It's good for humanity.

84
00:11:58,660 --> 00:12:05,710
Allah loves the ones who apologize the
most.

85
00:12:06,620 --> 00:12:07,730
But...

86
00:12:08,640 --> 00:12:11,620
there's people He loves more.

87
00:12:13,050 --> 00:12:18,290
The ones who apologize and
don't repeat the same fault.

88
00:12:19,660 --> 00:12:21,180
What about you, my Sheikh?

89
00:12:21,600 --> 00:12:23,430
Will you forgive me?

90
00:12:25,770 --> 00:12:28,820
We're not forgivers, Bala.

91
00:12:29,880 --> 00:12:33,670
Only Allah forgives.

92
00:12:34,850 --> 00:12:39,740
We only love and tolerate.

93
00:12:41,140 --> 00:12:45,720
And we love you for your honesty.

94
00:12:46,400 --> 00:12:51,240
We love you with your faults.

95
00:12:51,790 --> 00:12:53,490
You're our one and only.

96
00:12:53,850 --> 00:12:57,230
I thank Allah that He filled you
with cleverness...

97
00:12:57,890 --> 00:13:01,890
politeness and clean heart.

98
00:13:02,950 --> 00:13:06,950
We want you to preserve these.

99
00:13:07,670 --> 00:13:10,310
And we want this for you...

100
00:13:11,020 --> 00:13:13,450
not for us.

101
00:13:13,660 --> 00:13:15,250
Father...

102
00:13:18,480 --> 00:13:20,800
I love you.

103
00:13:21,400 --> 00:13:25,400
When you stand away from
me, my heart breaks.

104
00:13:31,470 --> 00:13:35,210
You're the gift and...

105
00:13:35,940 --> 00:13:38,660
entrustment of Allah to me.

106
00:13:39,540 --> 00:13:44,930
Your heart is clean. I know
your intention is good.

107
00:13:45,750 --> 00:13:47,460
From now on...

108
00:13:47,790 --> 00:13:51,380
I'm sure that you'll try not to...

109
00:13:51,660 --> 00:13:54,790
do bad things.

110
00:14:10,020 --> 00:14:12,660
You see, uncle?

111
00:14:14,680 --> 00:14:17,760
We're taken captured in our own land.

112
00:14:18,890 --> 00:14:22,890
This hurts the most.

113
00:14:24,300 --> 00:14:26,780
I couldn't save my brother's entrustments.

114
00:14:29,430 --> 00:14:30,890
I couldn't.

115
00:14:54,790 --> 00:14:59,750
Shahada or freedom.

116
00:15:31,780 --> 00:15:34,800
I'll adorn my weapon out of their corpses.

117
00:15:35,380 --> 00:15:37,210
Catch!

118
00:15:45,270 --> 00:15:46,930
Catch!

119
00:17:14,240 --> 00:17:16,030
Balgay wants Edebalı.

120
00:17:16,030 --> 00:17:19,800
We have to go to Bazaar. Come on!

121
00:17:30,760 --> 00:17:32,170
Come on!

122
00:18:40,730 --> 00:18:42,070
Allah!

123
00:18:45,750 --> 00:18:49,040
It's hard to serve the guests...

124
00:18:49,470 --> 00:18:53,470
as much as it is to ride
the vicious horse.

125
00:18:53,790 --> 00:18:58,590
I punched you out like a dog...

126
00:18:59,240 --> 00:19:03,070
so that you can enjoy my serve.

127
00:19:04,520 --> 00:19:09,860
Today, that jackal Osman have showed me that...

128
00:19:11,010 --> 00:19:14,130
if I let Turks breathe...

129
00:19:14,490 --> 00:19:18,490
your breathes become...

130
00:19:18,530 --> 00:19:20,830
Mongol blood.

131
00:19:21,020 --> 00:19:24,160
Raise your evil heads!

132
00:19:45,190 --> 00:19:46,300
Gündüz.

133
00:19:50,540 --> 00:19:51,570
Gündüz!

134
00:19:54,060 --> 00:19:55,310
Gündüz!

135
00:19:59,840 --> 00:20:01,290
My nephew.

136
00:20:01,980 --> 00:20:03,820
Gündüz...

137
00:20:04,080 --> 00:20:05,630
Now...

138
00:20:05,790 --> 00:20:07,910
tell me, Dündar Bey.

139
00:20:09,850 --> 00:20:17,840
Tell me one thing not to call out
Osman, who didn't obey me.

140
00:20:18,020 --> 00:20:19,580
Gündüz.

141
00:20:25,490 --> 00:20:26,840
Gündüz!

142
00:20:26,890 --> 00:20:28,410
Allah!

143
00:20:31,470 --> 00:20:32,870
Gündüz!

144
00:21:09,840 --> 00:21:12,890
- What is it?
- They raided the tribe.

145
00:21:12,920 --> 00:21:15,660
They captured Dündar Bey and Gündüz.

146
00:21:17,590 --> 00:21:19,920
Look what happened to us.

147
00:21:20,370 --> 00:21:22,950
- Help us, my Allah.

148
00:21:23,090 --> 00:21:27,090
Valiants, the day has come.

149
00:21:27,500 --> 00:21:31,370
We killed those cruels back then.

150
00:21:31,370 --> 00:21:34,110
Now, it's time to fight.

151
00:21:34,110 --> 00:21:38,110
Now, it's time to fight with
passion, with love.

152
00:21:38,110 --> 00:21:40,290
Not with anger.

153
00:21:40,350 --> 00:21:43,410
They came here to make my uncle and
my brother obey.

154
00:21:44,100 --> 00:21:47,460
Now, they will obey.

155
00:21:47,560 --> 00:21:51,090
Mongol aims at Edebalı.

156
00:21:51,090 --> 00:21:55,420
However, if they hurt Edebalı, that
means they kill our source of knowledge.

157
00:21:56,470 --> 00:21:57,910
My Osman!

158
00:21:57,940 --> 00:22:00,190
What are we waiting for?

159
00:22:02,100 --> 00:22:05,660
May our swords be blessed.

160
00:22:05,660 --> 00:22:08,320
Allahu-akbar ( Allah is the greatest)

161
00:22:08,380 --> 00:22:12,910
- Allahu-akbar (Allah is the greatest)
- Allahu-akbar (Allah is the greatest)

162
00:22:13,830 --> 00:22:15,220
Let's go!

163
00:22:24,940 --> 00:22:26,930
Gündüz!

164
00:22:35,530 --> 00:22:36,940
Osman.

165
00:22:38,630 --> 00:22:40,400
Osman is my nephew.

166
00:22:40,800 --> 00:22:44,800
He is young, he is zippy.

167
00:22:45,130 --> 00:22:50,730
We directly question the leader,
shepherd Dündar.

168
00:22:51,150 --> 00:22:54,690
Why didn't you inform your nephew
about Mongols' anger?

169
00:23:01,110 --> 00:23:05,720
We told him, but, he didn't listen.

170
00:23:08,070 --> 00:23:11,160
Gündüz has nothing to do with this.

171
00:23:11,320 --> 00:23:13,690
Don't kill my nephew.

172
00:23:13,700 --> 00:23:17,700
Give me a reason, Dündar.
Just one.

173
00:23:18,660 --> 00:23:21,760
We didn't know it could go this far.

174
00:23:22,670 --> 00:23:27,930
We didn't know Osman would get
out of hand.

175
00:23:38,790 --> 00:23:39,920
Gündüz.

176
00:23:45,630 --> 00:23:47,970
Then, know this.

177
00:23:47,970 --> 00:23:51,970
We came here with our ancestor
Cengiz's flames.

178
00:23:52,140 --> 00:23:55,750
We came here to destroy, to burn.

179
00:23:55,750 --> 00:23:59,750
If you make another mistake, I'll make
a drum...

180
00:24:00,240 --> 00:24:04,490
out of your skin and play it
in the Söğüt square.

181
00:24:13,750 --> 00:24:15,450
Gündüz.

182
00:24:20,920 --> 00:24:26,750
You'll obey me unconditionally, Dündar.

183
00:24:28,380 --> 00:24:32,380
Do you understand me?
Obey.

184
00:24:35,700 --> 00:24:37,700
I will...

185
00:24:38,660 --> 00:24:41,770
I will obey you.

186
00:24:47,770 --> 00:24:50,990
You will bring Osman to me.

187
00:24:51,950 --> 00:24:54,780
That way, you'll show your loyalty.

188
00:24:55,400 --> 00:24:59,180
I will bring Osman...

189
00:25:00,190 --> 00:25:01,850
to you.

190
00:25:03,400 --> 00:25:04,970
I will.

191
00:25:06,390 --> 00:25:08,540
You have three days.

192
00:25:08,950 --> 00:25:12,750
Or, I'll destroy your tribe.

193
00:25:14,380 --> 00:25:17,750
Now, take your nephew and...

194
00:25:17,910 --> 00:25:20,740
go back to your tribe and say:

195
00:25:20,890 --> 00:25:26,970
Mongols have come for good.

196
00:25:28,430 --> 00:25:33,160
Gündüz, Gündüz, my nephew.
Come on, get up.

197
00:25:33,350 --> 00:25:36,260
Come on, Bismillah. (in the name of Allah)
Gündüz, come on.

198
00:25:36,420 --> 00:25:38,470
Get up

199
00:25:41,500 --> 00:25:44,100
- Let's go.
- Take them out.

200
00:26:18,130 --> 00:26:20,680
Kayı's brave women.

201
00:26:21,220 --> 00:26:26,280
Today, we are not going to cry and
sit down.

202
00:26:26,700 --> 00:26:29,470
Today, we stand up and...

203
00:26:29,470 --> 00:26:33,730
show Mongol's the power
of Kayıs!

204
00:26:34,230 --> 00:26:38,230
Inform your sisters, they should take
positions outside.

205
00:26:38,230 --> 00:26:42,230
- We must be ready.
- Eyvallah (Okay) Selcan Hatun.

206
00:26:42,450 --> 00:26:46,250
It's not clear whether our men come
back or not, but...

207
00:26:46,410 --> 00:26:50,740
we know that the only return is to
Allah.

208
00:26:53,170 --> 00:26:56,040
Mongols will arrive at this tent.

209
00:26:56,120 --> 00:27:00,130
And we will show them that we
won't bow them!

210
00:27:00,190 --> 00:27:06,740
Let those dogs see that Kayı Hatuns
fight like Kayı men.

211
00:27:08,770 --> 00:27:13,180
I swear on our ancestors, Oguz's lands...

212
00:27:13,930 --> 00:27:17,930
- We won't bow!
- We won't bow!

213
00:27:18,190 --> 00:27:23,050
We will present death to those
who want to command Turks!

214
00:27:23,160 --> 00:27:24,790
We will!

215
00:27:24,950 --> 00:27:28,490
- Today, we fight!
- Today, we fight!

216
00:27:28,550 --> 00:27:33,990
- Today, we shahada!
- Today, we shahada!

217
00:27:35,430 --> 00:27:38,320
Ahis, who took shelter in Başkonuş plateau,
are ready.

218
00:27:38,330 --> 00:27:42,040
- They will take action with your command.
- Eyvallah (thank you)

219
00:27:42,210 --> 00:27:44,220
Thank them.

220
00:27:53,190 --> 00:27:55,560
- What is it?
- Balgay.

221
00:27:55,610 --> 00:27:57,910
He raided Söğüt with his soldiers,
my Sheik.

222
00:27:57,950 --> 00:28:01,270
He captured Dündar Bey and Gündüz Bey.

223
00:28:02,510 --> 00:28:06,950
He is being cruel.

224
00:28:08,090 --> 00:28:10,790
In Baqarah Surah, My Allah says...

225
00:28:11,440 --> 00:28:15,440
"And We will surely test you with
something of fear..."

226
00:28:15,650 --> 00:28:19,650
"and hunger and a loss of wealth..."

227
00:28:19,680 --> 00:28:23,970
"and lives and fruits..."

228
00:28:24,840 --> 00:28:33,000
"but give good tidings to the patient."
[Baqarah Surah 2:155]

229
00:28:36,310 --> 00:28:38,220
Zülfikar.

230
00:28:38,690 --> 00:28:40,990
Inform Ahis.

231
00:28:41,260 --> 00:28:43,780
We need to take precautions.

232
00:28:44,720 --> 00:28:47,550
Where are we going to go, my Sheik?

233
00:28:47,700 --> 00:28:49,530
Nowhere.

234
00:28:51,610 --> 00:28:53,630
We will stand up.

235
00:28:54,950 --> 00:28:57,760
If this state falls...

236
00:28:58,640 --> 00:29:02,640
it means there is no hope for Muslims.

237
00:29:04,020 --> 00:29:07,540
Mongols! Mongols are coming!

238
00:29:25,710 --> 00:29:28,180
I want Edebalı alive.

239
00:29:28,940 --> 00:29:30,470
Burn the rest.

240
00:29:30,470 --> 00:29:33,520
Come on, friends!

241
00:29:33,650 --> 00:29:36,520
Allahuekber! Allahuekber! (Allah is
the greatest)

242
00:30:32,920 --> 00:30:33,770
My Sheikh!

243
00:30:39,130 --> 00:30:40,250
My Sheikh!

244
00:30:54,400 --> 00:30:58,260
I want Edebalı alive. Burn the rest.

245
00:31:01,200 --> 00:31:02,470
Osman.

246
00:31:04,310 --> 00:31:05,940
I'm here, my Sheikh!

247
00:31:08,420 --> 00:31:09,510
Osman.

248
00:31:16,010 --> 00:31:19,020
Allah is eternal!

249
00:33:12,490 --> 00:33:15,080
Alps, we're going!

250
00:33:20,040 --> 00:33:22,030
Protect our Sheikh!

251
00:33:22,900 --> 00:33:26,870
My Bey, protect Sheikh Edebalı.
I'll deal with them.

252
00:33:31,660 --> 00:33:32,900
Come on.

253
00:34:00,160 --> 00:34:01,850
Don't kill him.

254
00:34:02,300 --> 00:34:03,970
I want him alive.

255
00:34:08,840 --> 00:34:10,460
I like you.

256
00:34:11,460 --> 00:34:13,130
You're my cup of tea.

257
00:34:13,330 --> 00:34:17,150
Be careful. I'm made of iron.

258
00:34:17,710 --> 00:34:19,230
Don't break your jaw.

259
00:34:20,640 --> 00:34:22,830
You saved them.

260
00:34:22,830 --> 00:34:26,420
Now tell me. Who will save you?

261
00:34:29,510 --> 00:34:31,810
Allah will.

262
00:34:48,510 --> 00:34:51,450
What were you saying in Alişar's mansion?

263
00:35:13,980 --> 00:35:15,790
I remembered.

264
00:35:21,140 --> 00:35:25,290
"I'm a witness!", you said.

265
00:35:28,610 --> 00:35:32,190
But you didn't witness
everything, Salvador.

266
00:35:33,520 --> 00:35:38,380
For example what my anger can do.

267
00:35:45,680 --> 00:35:47,110
There.

268
00:35:49,660 --> 00:35:51,370
You don't know.

269
00:36:34,400 --> 00:36:36,350
He can still make sounds!

270
00:36:41,410 --> 00:36:43,120
Good.

271
00:36:52,360 --> 00:36:53,910
Princess...

272
00:36:54,210 --> 00:36:55,710
Listen!

273
00:36:57,870 --> 00:36:59,770
Please explain.

274
00:37:02,970 --> 00:37:04,370
I'm listening.

275
00:37:10,450 --> 00:37:11,960
Princess...

276
00:37:33,560 --> 00:37:38,140
You said everything at the mansion!

277
00:37:39,080 --> 00:37:41,990
Now it's time to pay for them.

278
00:37:44,400 --> 00:37:47,080
As I'm bored...

279
00:37:48,220 --> 00:37:55,580
... I'll come here and rip your
fingernails off one by one!

280
00:38:04,550 --> 00:38:08,300
Stop. Stop! Stop!

281
00:38:10,470 --> 00:38:12,240
Princess!

282
00:38:13,040 --> 00:38:15,100
You don't know the big secret!

283
00:38:29,810 --> 00:38:31,630
Are you okay?

284
00:38:34,560 --> 00:38:38,370
Osman sent me here to gather information.

285
00:38:40,030 --> 00:38:42,460
He's waiting for my word.

286
00:39:00,330 --> 00:39:03,790
He... He'll give you the things you want.

287
00:39:05,950 --> 00:39:07,720
Think about it.

288
00:39:16,100 --> 00:39:19,880
Madam, this letter just came.

289
00:39:35,700 --> 00:39:37,210
Mongols.

290
00:39:38,590 --> 00:39:40,670
The letter is from Alişar.

291
00:39:40,860 --> 00:39:44,200
The Mongol commander Balgay will
be our guest, Helen.

292
00:39:47,720 --> 00:39:49,360
This dog...

293
00:39:52,350 --> 00:39:55,100
... should also talk to Master Yannis.

294
00:39:57,010 --> 00:39:58,760
Don't let him die!

295
00:40:03,090 --> 00:40:05,400
I'm the wolf of these mountains,
Osman Bey!

296
00:40:06,590 --> 00:40:08,680
Don't you worry!

297
00:40:09,100 --> 00:40:10,640
Sergeant Samsa.

298
00:40:13,560 --> 00:40:16,450
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.
( in the name of Allah, the merciful and compassionate.)

299
00:40:20,790 --> 00:40:22,970
O The Healer!

300
00:40:33,050 --> 00:40:34,810
It's ready, Osman Bey.

301
00:40:53,900 --> 00:40:57,120
Praise be, my valiant! Praise be!

302
00:41:05,920 --> 00:41:08,950
Fate protects one from their death.

303
00:41:10,170 --> 00:41:12,280
You're a godsend.

304
00:41:12,280 --> 00:41:15,390
Thankfully, Allah blessed us with you,
my Sheikh.

305
00:41:16,320 --> 00:41:18,810
Do you think they'll let brother
Konur live, my Bey?

306
00:42:00,810 --> 00:42:04,810
The taste of your blood tells
me that you're brave.

307
00:42:06,370 --> 00:42:08,980
But it's obvious that you're
not smart.

308
00:42:23,140 --> 00:42:29,090
All of you will pay the price for picking
on the Turks!

309
00:42:34,060 --> 00:42:38,060
I ask one question, I expect one answer,
you miserable Turk!

310
00:42:39,800 --> 00:42:42,340
Where is Osman?

311
00:42:42,500 --> 00:42:46,760
You look for him, but he'll find you.

312
00:42:47,080 --> 00:42:52,450
You'll see who the mountain and
who the hill is soon.

313
00:42:52,690 --> 00:42:54,720
Where is Osman?!

314
00:42:54,830 --> 00:42:56,510
He's where you'll die!

315
00:43:10,740 --> 00:43:13,930
They scared everyone.

316
00:43:15,500 --> 00:43:17,370
They discouraged everyone.

317
00:43:17,860 --> 00:43:19,800
They attacked the Tent too.

318
00:43:31,760 --> 00:43:35,060
The same goes for soldiers, doesn't it
Bamsı Bey?

319
00:43:35,150 --> 00:43:39,280
Someone who kills death, who makes
fear kneel...

320
00:43:39,760 --> 00:43:43,940
... who gives hope to his people, is
called a soldier.

321
00:43:47,820 --> 00:43:52,300
Let's see which valiant will shine
during this trial.

322
00:43:53,050 --> 00:43:55,730
Thank you, wise one. Thank you.

323
00:43:56,720 --> 00:44:03,460
Tell me. What is this valiant's quality
that will make him pass this trial?

324
00:44:03,610 --> 00:44:08,150
Not at all. This is a hard question,
Bamsı Bey.

325
00:44:09,200 --> 00:44:16,550
A man is a sufferer. First, he must
know which soil to plant his seed.

326
00:44:17,100 --> 00:44:21,690
He must know in which season he
should plant his seed.

327
00:44:29,300 --> 00:44:36,280
He must know when to water it, and how
to work the soil.

328
00:44:38,840 --> 00:44:44,170
He mustn't give a chance to the wild grass
which don't want the seed to sprout.

329
00:44:45,110 --> 00:44:48,270
While working on all of these...

330
00:44:48,270 --> 00:44:53,920
... he must not lose his love, his
nerve, his sincerity.

331
00:44:55,580 --> 00:44:59,160
One day, the seeds will sprout.

332
00:44:59,660 --> 00:45:01,510
He will harvest them.

333
00:45:02,640 --> 00:45:05,170
The goods will gain value.

334
00:45:05,940 --> 00:45:11,490
That day, this huge garden will not say
"These goods are mine!"

335
00:45:11,490 --> 00:45:14,610
..."They are my labour of love!",
Bamsı Bey.

336
00:45:16,540 --> 00:45:22,220
Whoever has such morals, such devotion...

337
00:45:23,100 --> 00:45:26,940
... My Allah will be that
valiant's friend.

338
00:45:32,160 --> 00:45:34,800
We'll be on their throats today!

339
00:45:35,330 --> 00:45:38,020
Söğüt will be their graves!

340
00:45:38,560 --> 00:45:41,200
We'll take our brother's revenge!

341
00:45:42,390 --> 00:45:45,860
Konur is stiff. He'll stand upright!

342
00:45:46,500 --> 00:45:48,120
He'll hold on!

343
00:46:00,550 --> 00:46:02,360
Sergeant Samsa!

344
00:46:03,530 --> 00:46:07,530
Osman Bey. There's no time to rest.

345
00:46:08,350 --> 00:46:12,530
Let's go and save Konur Alp.
I'm doing fine.

346
00:46:34,540 --> 00:46:36,240
Erkut, what is it?

347
00:46:36,800 --> 00:46:40,140
- New Bazaar's keeper Nizamettin.
- What about him?

348
00:46:40,140 --> 00:46:41,640
He's Yannis' servant, my Bey.

349
00:46:41,640 --> 00:46:45,190
Tell Master Yannis that Edebali's Ahis
will come from Engürü.

350
00:46:45,190 --> 00:46:47,850
Alişar Bey will do what's necessary
so Ahis don't come.

351
00:46:47,850 --> 00:46:50,850
You can go.
I'll dump their bodies in a river.

352
00:46:51,240 --> 00:46:54,040
Tell Master Yannis that his secret
is safe.

353
00:47:20,480 --> 00:47:22,100
Nizamettin!

354
00:47:33,890 --> 00:47:35,710
Hang on, my Dervish. Hang on.

355
00:47:35,710 --> 00:47:37,680
Where is Akça Dervish, son?

356
00:47:37,680 --> 00:47:40,740
I took him to Samsa Bey's Tent, my Sheikh.
He's safe.

357
00:47:43,340 --> 00:47:47,480
Tie Nizamettin's dead body to your horse
and send it so Söğüt.

358
00:47:47,750 --> 00:47:52,190
Send it so they can see who the real
owners of these lands are!

359
00:47:52,340 --> 00:47:54,180
As you wish, my Bey.

360
00:48:22,440 --> 00:48:25,110
- Where's Osman and Edebali?
- They ran away.

361
00:48:26,160 --> 00:48:28,150
That's bad news.

362
00:48:28,150 --> 00:48:31,910
You let the men who'll cause the most
trouble slip through your hands.

363
00:48:32,310 --> 00:48:35,320
No one runs away from the Mongol's
weapon, Alişar.

364
00:48:35,320 --> 00:48:38,130
They'll come out of their
holes eventually.

365
00:48:38,940 --> 00:48:41,120
You don't know them, Cerkutay

366
00:48:41,830 --> 00:48:43,890
They need to be found immediately.

367
00:48:44,050 --> 00:48:48,050
Don't you worry about them?
Commander Balgay is waiting for you.

368
00:48:58,100 --> 00:49:02,200
Pull yourselves together, mother. Aunt!

369
00:49:02,490 --> 00:49:04,760
We can't fight with them!

370
00:49:04,870 --> 00:49:09,030
Only an ambush for that dog
Balgay will shake them.

371
00:49:09,330 --> 00:49:12,570
- As long as there is such a valiant.
- Who's that valiant?

372
00:49:12,730 --> 00:49:17,490
Osman? We had such wise Beys once.

373
00:49:17,760 --> 00:49:21,000
Will Osman save us from
the Mongol thugs now?

374
00:49:21,390 --> 00:49:23,340
In these lands--

375
00:49:26,530 --> 00:49:27,910
My Bey!

376
00:49:29,980 --> 00:49:31,370
Father!

377
00:49:31,760 --> 00:49:33,380
What happened, my Bey?

378
00:49:33,380 --> 00:49:38,770
What do you think happened, Hatun?
The grim reaper is in our Tent.

379
00:49:39,240 --> 00:49:43,120
He'll take lives as he pleases.

380
00:49:58,130 --> 00:50:01,840
I'll eradicate this tumour which is
attacking our lands.

381
00:50:02,470 --> 00:50:05,900
I'll either honour these lands
or I'll die!

382
00:50:05,900 --> 00:50:09,010
We'll follow you wherever you go,
Head Alp.

383
00:50:11,330 --> 00:50:14,970
No, Kongun Alp. No.
I'll sort this one out myself.

384
00:50:15,230 --> 00:50:18,580
You stay by Dündar Bey while I'm not here.

385
00:50:33,330 --> 00:50:34,990
Where's Osman?

386
00:50:35,170 --> 00:50:39,170
He can do whatever he wants.
He's responsible for all of these!

387
00:50:41,890 --> 00:50:44,570
If you did what was necessary,
it wouldn't have happened.

388
00:50:44,570 --> 00:50:46,770
Shut up, Hatun! Shut up!

389
00:50:47,300 --> 00:50:50,700
- I don't want to deal with you too.
- Enough, Dündar Bey!

390
00:50:50,700 --> 00:50:53,210
Are you a valiant to me only?

391
00:50:53,440 --> 00:50:56,210
No one could deal with the Mongols.
How can we?

392
00:50:56,650 --> 00:51:02,340
If it's necessary for the Tent's safety,
give Osman to them!

393
00:51:06,290 --> 00:51:09,570
I can't destroy our families
just for Osman!

394
00:51:35,490 --> 00:51:44,350
Kulucahisar, then Bilecik, Yarhisarı,
and İnegöl governors, Commander Balgay.

395
00:51:45,930 --> 00:51:48,360
I want all of these castles, Alişar.

396
00:51:51,050 --> 00:51:53,760
All their soldiers are well-equipped.

397
00:51:55,070 --> 00:51:57,250
They reinforced their walls.

398
00:52:03,480 --> 00:52:07,330
I say I want Constantinople...

399
00:52:07,550 --> 00:52:12,090
... you show me the broken Byzantine
walls as obstacles.

400
00:52:16,570 --> 00:52:20,960
I have these castles' keys, Balgay.

401
00:52:27,330 --> 00:52:28,910
Sofia?

402
00:52:32,530 --> 00:52:37,620
She's so shameless that she'd sell
her ancestry to protect her lands.

403
00:52:38,870 --> 00:52:41,210
She's waiting for you in the castle.

404
00:52:44,370 --> 00:52:46,630
How will I benefit from her?

405
00:52:48,920 --> 00:52:54,470
Thanks to her, we'll sell our goods in
the Greek markets...

406
00:52:54,470 --> 00:52:56,550
... all the way to Constantinople.

407
00:52:57,860 --> 00:53:01,860
With the goods, your soldiers'
path will be opened.

408
00:53:02,630 --> 00:53:09,320
Step by step. One day they will wake up
and see that their walls are wracked.

409
00:53:18,590 --> 00:53:20,390
Sofia, huh?

410
00:53:23,730 --> 00:53:25,820
Is she beautiful?

411
00:53:26,960 --> 00:53:33,040
Shiny, like the moon. Sleek like
a pillar. Poisonous like a snake.

412
00:53:35,220 --> 00:53:40,190
If you take the wrong turn, you'll be
covered in mud, Alişar.

413
00:53:40,520 --> 00:53:42,210
Do you understand?

414
00:53:44,110 --> 00:53:47,710
I'll carry booty for you, Balgay.

415
00:53:47,710 --> 00:53:52,150
More booty than you ever saw in your life.

416
00:54:01,970 --> 00:54:06,740
Commander Balgay. Osman has sent
a gift for Alişar Bey.

417
00:54:08,820 --> 00:54:11,060
Ears lie, eyes are loyal.

418
00:54:14,880 --> 00:54:16,590
Let's see.

419
00:54:28,600 --> 00:54:30,560
Here, my Sheikh.

420
00:54:40,090 --> 00:54:42,370
Sharpen your swords, everyone!

421
00:54:42,370 --> 00:54:46,240
Today, they took one from us. Tomorrow,
we'll take a thousand from them!

422
00:54:48,200 --> 00:54:51,140
We'll make the Mongols regret
coming to these lands.

423
00:54:53,050 --> 00:54:56,310
I forgot my wounds because
of the pain in my heart.

424
00:54:56,670 --> 00:55:00,580
Let it hurt. Let it hurt.

425
00:55:00,740 --> 00:55:03,560
My flame burns brighter as it hurts!

426
00:55:04,820 --> 00:55:08,730
Those infidels are in our Tent,
and we're in this cave.

427
00:55:09,300 --> 00:55:12,510
- How can one stand this, my Bey?
- Relax.

428
00:55:14,390 --> 00:55:20,940
Our Prophet also hid in a cave
to escape from the infidels.

429
00:55:21,540 --> 00:55:28,490
Don't forget, valiants. There is a
cave Sevr for every truth to hide!

430
00:55:29,070 --> 00:55:35,070
Until the Mongol dogs grip the Turkish
ways, they can't leave these lands!

431
00:55:36,840 --> 00:55:41,120
But... Brother Konur is waiting for us.

432
00:55:41,690 --> 00:55:44,070
- Let's go.
- Stop, son!

433
00:55:46,660 --> 00:55:51,470
Once anger gets into one's heart,
he'll be out of his mind.

434
00:55:52,060 --> 00:55:54,500
- Don't rush!
- My Sheikh!

435
00:55:54,500 --> 00:55:57,780
Bamsı Bey! I can't let them
decide Konur's fate!

436
00:55:57,780 --> 00:56:00,960
- Osman!
- You know the Mongols the best!

437
00:56:00,960 --> 00:56:05,810
They are such snakes that they'll
use Konur to bite you!

438
00:56:06,010 --> 00:56:09,620
During hardships, you solve some problems
with swords in a field...

439
00:56:09,620 --> 00:56:13,710
... you solve others with being
a shadow in a corner.

440
00:56:16,190 --> 00:56:20,040
Bala! Go to the Kayı Tent
with Gonca in disguise.

441
00:56:20,040 --> 00:56:23,820
Your duty is being our eyes in the Tent.

442
00:56:26,470 --> 00:56:31,290
Bamsı Bey. Take Hatuns to the Tent.
I'll tell you what to do.

443
00:56:33,800 --> 00:56:35,480
Thank you, my Osman.

444
00:56:59,540 --> 00:57:02,930
Alişar brought these Mongols here, my Bey!

445
00:57:03,990 --> 00:57:09,190
Alişar will burn in this fire!
He'll burn!

446
00:57:41,350 --> 00:57:44,770
There was a Kayı arrow on
the body, Alişar Bey.

447
00:57:45,560 --> 00:57:48,230
It's certain that Osman did this.

448
00:57:51,530 --> 00:57:56,640
He's behind every trick
and every incident.

449
00:57:58,060 --> 00:58:03,320
I didn't know whom I trusted
these lands with.

450
00:58:09,060 --> 00:58:13,310
Osman! I'll bury you alive!

451
00:58:13,310 --> 00:58:18,660
I'll skin you with my bare hands, I'll
entertain ravens with your screams, Osman!

452
00:58:24,040 --> 00:58:26,170
Who is this?

453
00:58:26,350 --> 00:58:28,870
Manager of New Bazaar Nizamettin.

454
00:58:28,870 --> 00:58:31,300
What does Osman have to do with
a Bazaar officer?

455
00:58:32,500 --> 00:58:35,270
I think his goal is something else,
Commander Balgay.

456
00:58:35,270 --> 00:58:38,530
If that's the case, what are you
waiting for? Go find it out.

457
00:58:47,460 --> 00:58:50,580
What are your thoughts, Alişar Bey?

458
00:58:50,740 --> 00:58:55,910
No one in their right minds can
make sense of what he does.

459
00:59:02,220 --> 00:59:06,300
Didn't I tell you to look after every
branch, every corner...

460
00:59:06,300 --> 00:59:09,030
... every shadow of every Turk?

461
00:59:09,300 --> 00:59:11,840
Balgay! Balgay listen!

462
00:59:11,840 --> 00:59:15,070
Why should I listen to an
imbecile like you?

463
00:59:15,520 --> 00:59:20,900
You got my gold stolen. You brought
Kulucahisar and Kayıs to the brink of war.

464
00:59:20,900 --> 00:59:24,710
Is this how you treat the lands
I trusted you with?

465
00:59:26,210 --> 00:59:30,210
Balgay! Balgay, listen to me!
I'm begging you! Don't to it!

466
00:59:33,020 --> 00:59:34,760
I'm begging you! Don't do it!

467
00:59:37,230 --> 00:59:41,340
If you were my dog, you
couldn't bite my enemy.

468
00:59:43,600 --> 00:59:45,610
I don't want such a servant.

469
00:59:45,890 --> 00:59:46,950
No!

470
01:00:05,980 --> 01:00:07,830
Before you complete...

471
01:00:08,860 --> 01:00:12,860
... the job in Konya, don't you come back!

472
01:00:13,130 --> 01:00:15,910
- Balgay!
- You don't put a stone...

473
01:00:15,910 --> 01:00:18,210
... back to where you took it, Alişar.

474
01:00:18,780 --> 01:00:22,590
If you want to live, bring me some
good news.

475
01:00:24,440 --> 01:00:27,870
- Don't to it, Balgay!
- Are you still here?

476
01:00:56,620 --> 01:01:00,620
For now, the only use of you was
bringing Osman to me.

477
01:01:01,770 --> 01:01:05,770
The days which I'll make him kill
you are near, Alişar.

478
01:01:18,280 --> 01:01:21,850
What does Balgay want from you?
Did he say anything?

479
01:01:23,350 --> 01:01:25,850
He promised to make me the Banner Lord.

480
01:01:27,410 --> 01:01:33,330
His intention is obvious, my Sheikh.
He wants to scare us and loot us.

481
01:01:34,010 --> 01:01:38,010
He thinks that he can make me his ally.

482
01:01:41,670 --> 01:01:46,960
Since he saw that you won't submit to
power, he'll look for new allies.

483
01:01:47,440 --> 01:01:49,550
He'll do it with Alişar.

484
01:01:50,630 --> 01:01:53,920
Alişar will take Balgay to
the castle for sure.

485
01:01:58,710 --> 01:02:00,820
The sides have become clear, son.

486
01:02:02,230 --> 01:02:05,110
Dogs with dogs...

487
01:02:06,730 --> 01:02:09,660
... wolfs with wolfs!

488
01:02:23,310 --> 01:02:25,170
Welcome, Commander Balgay.

489
01:02:25,170 --> 01:02:27,630
Out of my way, imbecile!

490
01:02:30,080 --> 01:02:31,140
Stop!

491
01:02:53,410 --> 01:02:55,520
Princess Sofia is waiting for you.

492
01:02:59,350 --> 01:03:00,700
Here.

493
01:03:54,790 --> 01:03:58,500
White like the moon, sleek
like a pillar...

494
01:03:58,690 --> 01:04:01,400
... poisonous like a snake Sofia.
Is that you?

495
01:04:03,940 --> 01:04:07,080
Mighty Mongol Commander Balgay.

496
01:04:22,040 --> 01:04:24,210
Welcome to my castle.

497
01:04:36,170 --> 01:04:39,880
I thought Alişar Bey was also coming.

498
01:04:39,880 --> 01:04:42,220
I sent Alişar to Konya.

499
01:04:44,160 --> 01:04:48,400
But I didn't come empty-handed,
Princess Sofia.

500
01:04:53,240 --> 01:04:54,450
Yergutay.

501
01:05:16,180 --> 01:05:19,640
Nizamettin had been working
for you for a while.

502
01:05:23,330 --> 01:05:26,810
How did you come up with that,
Commander Balgay?

503
01:05:29,130 --> 01:05:33,130
What do I have to do with Alişar's
life long...

504
01:05:38,130 --> 01:05:39,280
... servant Nizamettin?

505
01:05:39,280 --> 01:05:40,630
Shut up!

506
01:05:40,990 --> 01:05:44,140
Until Osman sent this dog's dead
body as a gift...

507
01:05:44,750 --> 01:05:48,750
... Alişar who is as dumb as a
bird didn't know anything.

508
01:05:49,230 --> 01:05:53,050
Until I solved it with my mind.

509
01:05:59,790 --> 01:06:03,790
Akça Dervish was your biggest enemy
Edebali's man.

510
01:06:05,390 --> 01:06:11,170
Alişar was licking that old man's boots
just so he could be with his daughter.

511
01:06:12,720 --> 01:06:15,330
It's certain he didn't make them do it.

512
01:06:29,970 --> 01:06:33,100
They don't call you the mighty
Commander for nothing.

513
01:06:34,250 --> 01:06:38,100
Why did you want to make your spy
kill the Dervish, Sofia?

514
01:06:38,890 --> 01:06:43,130
Did he see something you were hiding in
Alişar's mansion or did he see anyone?

515
01:06:43,130 --> 01:06:46,410
Edebali is our enemy as much as
he's your enemy.

516
01:06:47,440 --> 01:06:54,090
Our common enemies will make
agreeing with you easier.

517
01:06:54,860 --> 01:06:57,410
I didn't come here to make an agreement.

518
01:07:10,610 --> 01:07:14,080
I came here to make you
my bondwoman(Female servant)!

519
01:07:38,930 --> 01:07:41,730
Not in Kulucahisar...

520
01:07:43,250 --> 01:07:47,540
... I'll let you make me your
bondwoman in Constantinople.

521
01:07:54,570 --> 01:07:55,890
Balgay.

522
01:07:57,910 --> 01:07:59,350
I like you.

523
01:07:59,850 --> 01:08:01,240
You are an intelligent woman.

524
01:08:01,690 --> 01:08:02,730
You are ambitious...

525
01:08:03,170 --> 01:08:05,170
...charming and determined.

526
01:08:22,880 --> 01:08:24,890
I had the table prepared for you.

527
01:08:27,100 --> 01:08:27,850
After you.

528
01:08:29,220 --> 01:08:31,930
Only the Byzantine cockroaches eat on a
table.

529
01:08:33,250 --> 01:08:36,860
A Mongolian who eats at a table is
an open target for his enemies.

530
01:08:39,390 --> 01:08:41,130
I came here to talk about
business...

531
01:08:42,070 --> 01:08:45,320
... or to destroy your castle.

532
01:08:54,700 --> 01:08:56,470
Söğüt has four gates.

533
01:08:57,350 --> 01:09:00,320
Balgay put his guards here.

534
01:09:01,640 --> 01:09:03,370
And we will infiltrate from there...

535
01:09:03,650 --> 01:09:06,570
... from behind the Bazaar to this
point.

536
01:09:09,100 --> 01:09:10,650
Understood, Osman Bey.

537
01:09:11,200 --> 01:09:13,680
But this means we have to fight our way
to exit.

538
01:09:15,240 --> 01:09:18,560
Those locusts will attack us as soon as
one of them smells us.

539
01:09:20,570 --> 01:09:21,350
Boran.

540
01:09:22,240 --> 01:09:24,450
Söğüt is our earned right.

541
01:09:27,230 --> 01:09:31,310
It doesn't matter if clash against Genghis
Khan or Balgay. We'll win.

542
01:09:34,130 --> 01:09:38,130
After the Mongolians, we will show the
whole world that blood is what they get...

543
01:09:38,220 --> 01:09:42,500
...when they mess with the Turks.

544
01:09:46,940 --> 01:09:50,520
What do you want from your
Princess Sofia, Commander Balgay?

545
01:10:09,830 --> 01:10:14,060
As a result of my negotiating skills,
along with the every beauty inside...

546
01:10:14,060 --> 01:10:16,060
...I took over the control of Kulacahisar.

547
01:10:16,330 --> 01:10:17,860
This castle is mine now.

548
01:10:18,780 --> 01:10:22,180
Now you'll give me the other
governor's castles.

549
01:10:23,770 --> 01:10:24,960
Do you understand?

550
01:10:26,850 --> 01:10:27,760
Exceedingly.

551
01:10:31,800 --> 01:10:34,970
Since Balgay's strong hands...

552
01:10:34,970 --> 01:10:37,740
... know where to take me...

553
01:10:41,470 --> 01:10:43,800
It is my duty to...

554
01:10:46,160 --> 01:10:48,470
...serve the hand that I
could not bend.

555
01:11:31,190 --> 01:11:37,790
Along with my soldiers, I'm ready to obey
with my flesh and soul, Commander Balgay.

556
01:11:57,350 --> 01:12:02,020
Then, I raise my sword that has been
washed with Turkish blood...

557
01:12:03,180 --> 01:12:04,490
... for my Queen.

558
01:12:19,330 --> 01:12:20,220
Ayşe!

559
01:12:20,560 --> 01:12:21,500
Ayşe!

560
01:12:21,740 --> 01:12:24,860
I can no longer stand the responsibilities
of Zöhre. Dündar Bey...

561
01:12:24,860 --> 01:12:26,190
... is a coward himself.

562
01:12:26,190 --> 01:12:27,890
They blame my Osman for everything.

563
01:12:27,910 --> 01:12:31,360
They think if Osman had obeyed Alişar just
like they did...

564
01:12:31,410 --> 01:12:32,890
... none of these would happen.

565
01:12:32,900 --> 01:12:36,110
There is no way Osman would allow the
honor of Kayı lay on the ground.

566
01:12:36,110 --> 01:12:37,490
What are we going to do?

567
01:12:37,600 --> 01:12:39,000
If we don't do anything...

568
01:12:39,020 --> 01:12:41,210
...they will hand Osman to the Mongolians.

569
01:12:41,230 --> 01:12:42,330
We have three days.

570
01:12:43,210 --> 01:12:44,660
May Allah be with us.

571
01:12:50,290 --> 01:12:51,320
My aunt.

572
01:12:52,760 --> 01:12:54,770
How are you, Selcan Hatun.

573
01:12:55,550 --> 01:12:59,220
How we are is basically a Tent that
submits to the power of the Mongols.

574
01:12:59,780 --> 01:13:01,310
There are no news from my Osman.

575
01:13:01,650 --> 01:13:03,270
My heart feels like it is on fire.

576
01:13:03,580 --> 01:13:05,220
Don't worry, Sercan Hatun.

577
01:13:05,420 --> 01:13:06,690
Osman is fine.

578
01:13:08,240 --> 01:13:09,320
You don't say!

579
01:13:09,470 --> 01:13:10,420
Where is he?

580
01:13:10,420 --> 01:13:11,970
I hope his condition is alright.

581
01:13:11,980 --> 01:13:13,360
I will tell you everything.

582
01:13:13,650 --> 01:13:16,340
Now tell me. What is going on?

583
01:13:19,160 --> 01:13:21,450
Balgay wants my Osman.

584
01:13:22,130 --> 01:13:24,190
Dündar won't say anything against it.

585
01:13:24,260 --> 01:13:26,540
He is okay with giving Osman away.

586
01:13:28,250 --> 01:13:30,140
He gave us three days, Bala Hatun.

587
01:13:31,180 --> 01:13:35,410
He said he will burn down the Tent
if Osman doesn't come back in three days.

588
01:13:38,290 --> 01:13:40,190
You stay here my dear.

589
01:13:40,550 --> 01:13:41,960
I will tell them news.

590
01:13:41,960 --> 01:13:43,380
You should leave, Gonca.

591
01:13:43,390 --> 01:13:45,090
There is no time to waste.

592
01:13:50,390 --> 01:13:53,030
Osman is holding his ground with Edebali.

593
01:13:54,800 --> 01:13:57,440
With the help of Allah, they will defeat
the Mongols.

594
01:13:58,180 --> 01:14:02,110
We will either walk on our path free or
recite the Kalima Shahadah.

595
01:14:03,240 --> 01:14:04,350
If Allah allows us.

596
01:14:06,190 --> 01:14:08,140
However, nobody can know that I was here.

597
01:14:08,520 --> 01:14:10,370
Don't you worry, my beautiful girl.

598
01:14:10,580 --> 01:14:13,370
You came here and calmed our worried
minds.

599
01:14:13,510 --> 01:14:15,800
Because of you my heart is finally at
peace.

600
01:14:23,720 --> 01:14:25,540
Alişar has fallen from the game.

601
01:14:27,550 --> 01:14:29,520
Now, the new King is Balgay.

602
01:14:30,990 --> 01:14:37,560
Don't you ever forget that even a simple
pawn can beat the King, Sofia.

603
01:14:47,550 --> 01:14:48,700
Checkmate.

604
01:14:52,020 --> 01:14:53,930
Osman is now a living dead.

605
01:14:54,510 --> 01:14:58,510
If he doesn't surrender, Balgay will
destroy the whole Tent.

606
01:14:59,980 --> 01:15:01,700
Edebali has left the Bazaar.

607
01:15:05,310 --> 01:15:07,930
As soon as Balgay finds them, he will
take their heads.

608
01:15:07,990 --> 01:15:11,220
Now, there is not even a single branch
that Ahis can hold.

609
01:15:15,940 --> 01:15:19,600
However, there is one thing. Father.
How are we going to get rid of Balgay?

610
01:15:20,540 --> 01:15:22,470
Everyone has a weakness, my daughter.

611
01:15:23,600 --> 01:15:25,830
And I know Balgay's weakness the best.

612
01:15:31,630 --> 01:15:33,250
Where are you going to go, father?

613
01:15:34,000 --> 01:15:36,310
It's time I pay a visit to Balgay.

614
01:15:37,180 --> 01:15:40,480
Thanks to you, now we know what exactly he
wants.

615
01:15:42,390 --> 01:15:44,590
You are going to give him what he wants.

616
01:15:48,030 --> 01:15:50,270
May God protect you, Master Yannis.

617
01:16:14,120 --> 01:16:15,360
Dündar Bey.

618
01:16:16,360 --> 01:16:18,540
Ever since you became in charge of the
Tent...

619
01:16:18,540 --> 01:16:20,200
...there is nothing but trouble.

620
01:16:20,370 --> 01:16:22,560
Now, the Mongols are here.

621
01:16:22,700 --> 01:16:24,430
What do those tyrants want my Bey?

622
01:16:25,340 --> 01:16:27,060
They gave us three days.

623
01:16:28,410 --> 01:16:31,390
They want to capture Osman.

624
01:16:36,640 --> 01:16:39,420
All of these oppressions and torments we
are going through.

625
01:16:39,420 --> 01:16:40,470
Does Osman worth it?

626
01:16:40,910 --> 01:16:43,010
Let's hand him and be done with them
already.

627
01:16:43,870 --> 01:16:46,730
Don't talk as if you are giving away
a sheep from your herb.

628
01:16:48,910 --> 01:16:51,270
Osman is the only thing that my father
left me.

629
01:16:51,270 --> 01:16:52,440
What about our children?

630
01:16:53,390 --> 01:16:55,260
What about them, Gündüz Bey?

631
01:16:55,580 --> 01:16:59,110
A Bey always takes care after his Tent no
matter what.

632
01:17:00,060 --> 01:17:04,550
Not only Osman but also I would not give
even a single cloth piece from this Tent.

633
01:17:05,320 --> 01:17:07,760
Are we going to sacrifice the whole Tent
for Osman?

634
01:17:07,770 --> 01:17:09,170
It's not about Osman!

635
01:17:10,160 --> 01:17:11,640
It's about our freedom!

636
01:17:13,150 --> 01:17:14,580
Why can't you understand?

637
01:17:14,900 --> 01:17:16,780
Then you better get this, Gündüz Bey.

638
01:17:17,090 --> 01:17:20,590
A certain herb does not feed on freedom
and empty promises.

639
01:17:22,810 --> 01:17:26,810
How can we let our enemy walk freely in
our own land?

640
01:17:29,310 --> 01:17:30,720
We are the Kayıs!

641
01:17:31,540 --> 01:17:35,830
We shout "Freedom!" to these mountains,
and they shout back "Allahu Akbar!"

642
01:17:36,110 --> 01:17:37,900
What kind of an intimidation this is?

643
01:17:37,960 --> 01:17:38,810
You bloodless!

644
01:17:41,600 --> 01:17:42,300
Enough!

645
01:17:44,770 --> 01:17:45,850
Enough.

646
01:18:04,520 --> 01:18:05,720
How childish of you!

647
01:18:06,840 --> 01:18:09,710
This is not who we are.

648
01:18:10,410 --> 01:18:11,340
Behave yourselves!

649
01:18:11,670 --> 01:18:13,150
You are all acting like Beys...

650
01:18:13,150 --> 01:18:16,100
...as if you can't see there is already a
Bey here at his council.

651
01:18:17,200 --> 01:18:18,520
Sit down! All of you!

652
01:18:44,460 --> 01:18:48,310
It is not the time we sit but the time we
do what our customs dictate, Dündar bey.

653
01:18:49,940 --> 01:18:53,760
Tell us your last decision already so
that we can understand your motive.

654
01:18:58,840 --> 01:19:02,950
My decision is as obvious as the wildness
of the Mongols.

655
01:19:05,400 --> 01:19:12,540
Especially since our customs strongly
dictate we need to stand together.

656
01:19:16,280 --> 01:19:20,280
We'll wait for Osman and try not to end
in such conflicts again.

657
01:19:22,270 --> 01:19:24,400
What if he doesn't come back, Dündar Bey?

658
01:19:26,030 --> 01:19:29,560
While you constantly worry about your
children...

659
01:19:29,560 --> 01:19:33,840
...we are always sure of ours, Demirci
Bey.

660
01:19:36,820 --> 01:19:41,190
Sometimes, Osman might be a bit crazy
and full of youth.

661
01:19:41,190 --> 01:19:43,560
However, he knows what he is doing.

662
01:19:43,560 --> 01:19:45,920
He would never leave his Tent alone.

663
01:19:45,920 --> 01:19:50,390
Not even a single second he would
hesitate to help his people.

664
01:19:50,390 --> 01:19:53,400
No matter what, he would grab his sword
and find a way to help.

665
01:20:26,830 --> 01:20:29,270
Is our old friend here?

666
01:20:29,610 --> 01:20:31,170
He will arrive soon sir.

667
01:21:47,060 --> 01:21:50,220
One of the Margaret monks, Yannis.

668
01:21:51,910 --> 01:21:53,740
It's been years.

669
01:21:53,860 --> 01:21:56,380
You see? Finally we meet once again.

670
01:21:57,030 --> 01:21:59,790
I came here to put an end to our
unfinished business.

671
01:22:03,680 --> 01:22:05,110
Sheikh Edebali.

672
01:22:05,870 --> 01:22:12,510
We will kill him just like how we killed
Ahi Evran together.

673
01:22:19,170 --> 01:22:21,270
What did you bring me, Yannis?

674
01:22:35,300 --> 01:22:36,840
What are these names?

675
01:22:36,840 --> 01:22:37,930
Who are they?

676
01:22:37,990 --> 01:22:41,230
Bilecik, Inegöl, and Harmankaya.

677
01:22:42,320 --> 01:22:45,320
Names of all monks and people who
are devoted to me...

678
01:22:45,320 --> 01:22:47,100
...and live at these very casttles.

679
01:22:47,510 --> 01:22:49,300
Some of them are castle commanders.

680
01:22:49,820 --> 01:22:51,170
Some of them are soldiers.

681
01:22:51,900 --> 01:22:53,110
Some of them are doctors.

682
01:22:53,510 --> 01:22:54,490
Cooks.

683
01:22:54,490 --> 01:22:55,400
Stablemen.

684
01:22:55,750 --> 01:23:02,210
With a single order from me, they will be
ready to serve you.

685
01:23:07,710 --> 01:23:09,920
What is the reason behind this, Yannis?

686
01:23:10,390 --> 01:23:11,520
For my daughter.

687
01:23:12,560 --> 01:23:13,510
Your daughter?

688
01:23:13,770 --> 01:23:14,960
Sofia!

689
01:23:17,160 --> 01:23:20,480
I came here to present you...

690
01:23:20,480 --> 01:23:22,860
...a very beautiful Princess...

691
01:23:22,860 --> 01:23:26,060
...along with Constantinople, Balgay.

692
01:23:35,680 --> 01:23:41,720
Our ancestors told us to eat high
quality meat always...

693
01:23:41,720 --> 01:23:45,720
...and to listen to the words of old men.

694
01:23:50,280 --> 01:23:54,230
If I don't like the meat you serve with
your daughter...

695
01:23:54,230 --> 01:23:57,030
...both of you will drown in my puke,
Yannis.

696
01:23:57,340 --> 01:23:59,510
Don't you ever forget this.

697
01:24:09,050 --> 01:24:11,950
To his almighty Genghis Khan...

698
01:24:11,950 --> 01:24:13,140
...and his breed.

699
01:25:41,170 --> 01:25:43,510
They keep Konur inside the church.

700
01:25:44,410 --> 01:25:45,520
My Bey.

701
01:25:45,700 --> 01:25:47,270
They are probably waiting for us.

702
01:25:48,140 --> 01:25:49,490
You should wait here.

703
01:25:49,750 --> 01:25:51,570
I will go rescue Konur and come back.

704
01:25:52,080 --> 01:25:54,650
However, we might have to clash as
soon as we are out.

705
01:26:10,850 --> 01:26:13,130
We need to stay alert, my brothers.

706
01:26:13,620 --> 01:26:15,630
Understood, Samsa Bey.

707
01:26:23,440 --> 01:26:24,500
Konur!

708
01:26:54,850 --> 01:26:56,970
Where have you been, Osman bey?

709
01:27:29,620 --> 01:27:30,800
Drop your swords!

710
01:28:27,960 --> 01:28:29,930
Osman Bey, it's an ambush!

711
01:28:32,290 --> 01:28:34,270
Be careful, my Osman Bey.

712
01:28:48,690 --> 01:28:50,890
I will choke all of you on your own blood.

713
01:28:51,600 --> 01:28:55,280
You are not different from our past foes
whom we fed our dogs with.

714
01:28:57,570 --> 01:28:58,470
Come at me!

715
01:29:30,780 --> 01:29:32,580
Leave this place, Osman Bey!

716
01:30:31,840 --> 01:30:33,110
Find Osman!

717
01:30:56,990 --> 01:30:57,890
Stop!

718
01:31:10,750 --> 01:31:12,680
It's the end of the road, Balgay.

719
01:31:14,780 --> 01:31:15,560
Come.

720
01:31:16,240 --> 01:31:17,300
And fight.

721
01:31:27,300 --> 01:31:31,730
Do you know what happens when a dog acts
like a wolf, son of Dündar?

722
01:31:41,450 --> 01:31:45,850
He will be executed in front of other
dogs...

723
01:31:45,870 --> 01:31:48,300
...so that they can learn their lessons.

724
01:32:04,660 --> 01:32:05,880
Commander Balgay.

725
01:32:07,570 --> 01:32:08,810
Osman has just fled.

726
01:32:11,450 --> 01:32:13,510
However, his Alps are our prisoners now.

727
01:32:14,460 --> 01:32:16,310
He will come back for his dogs.

728
01:32:17,360 --> 01:32:19,690
We will go this time, Kongar.

729
01:32:22,380 --> 01:32:25,710
We will have a blood fest at Kayı's Tent.

730
01:32:26,270 --> 01:32:30,600
They will learn to surrender.

731
01:33:17,450 --> 01:33:19,820
What did they do to you, Konur brother?

732
01:33:22,730 --> 01:33:25,020
Your face is barely recognizable.

733
01:33:31,050 --> 01:33:32,230
Is that so?

734
01:33:33,390 --> 01:33:34,520
I don't agree.

735
01:33:35,890 --> 01:33:37,100
I feel like a lion.

736
01:33:37,820 --> 01:33:38,630
A lion?

737
01:33:39,920 --> 01:33:41,220
More like a wounded lion.

738
01:33:49,400 --> 01:33:51,690
Stop messing with me, Sergeant Samsa.

739
01:33:52,920 --> 01:33:55,510
My brother has always been like a lion.

740
01:33:56,060 --> 01:33:58,290
Nothing can harm him.

741
01:34:00,510 --> 01:34:02,780
I'm not real lion around here.

742
01:34:06,030 --> 01:34:07,440
He is the real lion.

743
01:34:08,870 --> 01:34:09,770
My dear brother.

744
01:34:10,970 --> 01:34:19,390
To Pharaohs, cruels, infidels, he once
again showed us how to stand...

745
01:34:19,390 --> 01:34:23,850
... against our enemies with bravery,
not with our bulk.

746
01:34:25,790 --> 01:34:26,700
My lion.

747
01:34:32,060 --> 01:34:33,760
What's wrong, Abdurrahman brother?

748
01:34:34,520 --> 01:34:35,980
You seem dreamy again.

749
01:34:36,660 --> 01:34:39,090
We learned how to fight like a real man...

750
01:34:39,090 --> 01:34:41,450
...what it means to be brothers in arms...

751
01:34:41,450 --> 01:34:44,480
...from those like you whose beard turned
to gray...

752
01:34:44,480 --> 01:34:46,650
...because of fighting non-stop
for his Tent.

753
01:34:46,800 --> 01:34:48,450
I drifted away.

754
01:34:49,310 --> 01:34:52,940
I just fear that a valiant like
Osman Bey...

755
01:34:52,940 --> 01:34:55,460
...might be captivated because of us.

756
01:34:55,460 --> 01:34:57,720
May Allah not allow that, Abdurrahman
brother.

757
01:34:57,790 --> 01:34:59,890
Amin.

758
01:35:00,110 --> 01:35:01,270
Samsa Bey.

759
01:35:02,250 --> 01:35:03,730
What are we going to do now?

760
01:35:03,860 --> 01:35:05,640
Don't get nervous, my Boran.

761
01:35:07,330 --> 01:35:10,130
La Ghalib illa Allah.
(There is no victor/conqueror except God)

762
01:35:10,790 --> 01:35:12,550
Amin.

763
01:35:15,020 --> 01:35:16,870
Didn't we promise...

764
01:35:16,870 --> 01:35:21,410
...that as long as we are alive and we
have our swords with us...

765
01:35:21,410 --> 01:35:23,770
...we won't become exhausted...

766
01:35:23,770 --> 01:35:24,770
...hopeless...

767
01:35:24,770 --> 01:35:26,250
...or afraid of anything...

768
01:35:26,250 --> 01:35:32,300
...that we will never surrender and die
if it is necessary to protect our Tent.

769
01:35:33,130 --> 01:35:34,700
Didn't we, Konur Brother?

770
01:35:35,110 --> 01:35:36,470
Huh, Boran Brother?

771
01:35:36,920 --> 01:35:38,480
Yes, we all promised that.

772
01:35:38,790 --> 01:35:40,340
We did, Sergeant Samsa.

773
01:35:42,550 --> 01:35:46,780
Let the tyrants be tyrants.

774
01:35:46,810 --> 01:35:48,560
Let them be a kind of nightmare.

775
01:35:48,560 --> 01:35:51,360
Let them slay every single one of us.

776
01:35:51,500 --> 01:35:56,460
What is important is to know that our
blood, swords, and words...

777
01:35:56,460 --> 01:35:58,280
...can not be changed.

778
01:36:02,410 --> 01:36:05,360
After all, we can't change our destiny.

779
01:36:06,850 --> 01:36:09,790
There is nothing but to
accept the shahada, Allah's power.

780
01:36:10,850 --> 01:36:12,980
Allahu Akbar!

781
01:36:13,470 --> 01:36:14,930
Allahu Akbar!

782
01:36:15,350 --> 01:36:16,320
Allahu Akbar!

783
01:36:17,560 --> 01:36:18,660
Allahu Akbar!

784
01:36:20,140 --> 01:36:21,250
Allahu Akbar!

785
01:36:21,990 --> 01:36:30,580
Allahu Akbar!

786
01:36:33,800 --> 01:36:34,890
My friends.

787
01:36:35,580 --> 01:36:37,270
Listen to me carefully now.

788
01:36:45,030 --> 01:36:45,880
Gonca Hatun.

789
01:36:47,410 --> 01:36:48,770
You ought to tell me!

790
01:36:50,100 --> 01:36:52,000
How's the Tent doing?

791
01:36:54,770 --> 01:36:56,420
It's doing bad, Osman Bey.

792
01:36:57,760 --> 01:36:59,150
It's doing bad.

793
01:37:00,480 --> 01:37:01,800
It wants you back.

794
01:37:04,750 --> 01:37:07,270
Dündar Bey had to submit to others.

795
01:37:12,530 --> 01:37:14,860
If you don't surrender in three days.

796
01:37:51,580 --> 01:37:53,840
We lost everything, my Sheikh.

797
01:37:55,790 --> 01:37:56,500
Osman!

798
01:37:56,840 --> 01:37:58,870
All of Söğüt is under attack.

799
01:38:00,780 --> 01:38:02,760
They raided every Tent there is.

800
01:38:03,820 --> 01:38:05,640
All Beys are taken prisoners.

801
01:38:07,950 --> 01:38:08,650
Osman!

802
01:38:09,980 --> 01:38:11,490
They got my Alps as well.

803
01:38:13,400 --> 01:38:14,130
Osman!

804
01:38:14,720 --> 01:38:15,620
Stand up!

805
01:38:22,490 --> 01:38:23,330
Stand up!

806
01:38:39,630 --> 01:38:41,990
I want to tell you an anecdote.

807
01:38:42,010 --> 01:38:44,620
An anecdote from Battle of Uhud.

808
01:38:44,640 --> 01:38:48,840
So that you can understand what real
responsibility and hope mean.

809
01:38:51,380 --> 01:38:56,120
That day when Muslims and non-believers
started to clash...

810
01:38:56,840 --> 01:39:00,870
...do you think all that was easy?

811
01:39:01,580 --> 01:39:06,460
Almost three hundred soldiers left
our prophet's side.

812
01:39:07,570 --> 01:39:10,050
His cheek was wounded by a sword dash.

813
01:39:10,360 --> 01:39:12,250
His lips got torn by the stones...

814
01:39:12,250 --> 01:39:13,920
...and some of his teeth got
broken.

815
01:39:14,890 --> 01:39:18,220
After another sword dash...

816
01:39:18,220 --> 01:39:21,040
...blood was
dripping from his blessed forehead.

817
01:39:21,960 --> 01:39:24,400
While he was going back to Mecca...

818
01:39:24,400 --> 01:39:27,700
...he fell into one of
the ditches dug by the heathens.

819
01:39:28,300 --> 01:39:29,990
His knee was torn this time.

820
01:39:30,320 --> 01:39:33,160
He lost too many comrades.

821
01:39:33,160 --> 01:39:35,000
He even lost...

822
01:39:35,000 --> 01:39:37,340
...the lion of Allah...

823
01:39:37,340 --> 01:39:39,790
...his uncle, Hamza,...

824
01:39:39,790 --> 01:39:41,690
...on that battle.

825
01:39:42,750 --> 01:39:45,810
After everything that happened to him.
He could still say that...

826
01:39:45,810 --> 01:39:48,180
''My Rab please have mercy on them.''

827
01:39:48,180 --> 01:39:50,620
''They don't know about the truth.''

828
01:39:53,730 --> 01:39:56,460
Do you know why all of these happened, my
son?

829
01:39:58,270 --> 01:40:00,350
Because...

830
01:40:00,350 --> 01:40:02,870
... some of his soldiers...

831
01:40:03,820 --> 01:40:05,650
... did not complete his orders.

832
01:40:08,090 --> 01:40:12,930
The believers who had seen the heathens
flee away...

833
01:40:13,290 --> 01:40:17,290
... left their spot too soon
to get their loot.

834
01:40:19,410 --> 01:40:21,030
Don't you forget, my son.

835
01:40:23,660 --> 01:40:28,610
This anecdote is one of the most important
doctrines of archaic history of Islam.

836
01:40:29,510 --> 01:40:31,920
When the believers are scattered around...

837
01:40:32,020 --> 01:40:33,850
... the heathens will start to riot.

838
01:40:40,840 --> 01:40:43,290
Now, your duty is...

839
01:40:43,290 --> 01:40:48,120
...not to scatter around but to pull
yourself and everything together.

840
01:40:51,010 --> 01:40:57,470
Now, Kayı Tent is that spot where the
believers left too soon.

841
01:40:59,400 --> 01:41:01,530
If we leave the spot...

842
01:41:01,680 --> 01:41:05,680
... the heathens will try to strike more
stronger than ever.

843
01:41:07,330 --> 01:41:10,470
Now claim your Tent...

844
01:41:10,480 --> 01:41:12,570
...your people and your cause...

845
01:41:12,570 --> 01:41:14,330
...stronger than ever.

846
01:41:14,510 --> 01:41:18,510
So that the Muslims can riot against the
heathens once again.

847
01:41:28,940 --> 01:41:31,690
I am flattered and full of hope again, my
Sheikh.

848
01:41:43,680 --> 01:41:44,610
Gonca Hatun.

849
01:41:45,660 --> 01:41:47,670
You better listen to me carefully.

850
01:41:48,290 --> 01:41:51,790
Go to the Tent to my aunt Selcan.

851
01:42:09,280 --> 01:42:10,820
Traitors!

852
01:42:11,960 --> 01:42:14,060
You are all traitors!

853
01:42:22,600 --> 01:42:24,740
You are all traitors!

854
01:42:29,060 --> 01:42:30,770
Allah!

855
01:43:02,450 --> 01:43:04,180
Allah!

856
01:43:23,030 --> 01:43:25,140
- Batur!
- Brother!

857
01:43:26,080 --> 01:43:28,030
Let go of me, Bey!

858
01:43:28,030 --> 01:43:29,500
Hatun!

859
01:43:54,320 --> 01:43:59,980
Here is Cengiz Han's soul!

860
01:44:00,390 --> 01:44:02,750
Balgay is here!

861
01:44:13,380 --> 01:44:15,100
My Allah.

862
01:44:19,230 --> 01:44:23,850
Stand tall, my lions! Don't make the enemy
happy! Stand tall!

863
01:44:25,990 --> 01:44:28,090
Now...

864
01:44:28,440 --> 01:44:30,370
We will...

865
01:44:30,370 --> 01:44:34,280
make these dogs obey!

866
01:44:39,650 --> 01:44:41,190
Allah!

867
01:44:46,700 --> 01:44:50,980
Don't bow to the cruel!

868
01:44:52,570 --> 01:44:56,840
Come on, brothers, alps!
Hold on!

869
01:44:57,100 --> 01:44:58,810
Allah!

870
01:46:06,940 --> 01:46:11,230
The truth is the same with a sharp knife.

871
01:46:14,680 --> 01:46:19,020
I brought you the captivity.

872
01:46:42,850 --> 01:46:47,120
May you strengthen us, my Allah.
Amin.

873
01:46:51,320 --> 01:46:53,920
Obviously, you forgot.

874
01:46:55,120 --> 01:46:56,970
I'll make it clear.

875
01:46:57,680 --> 01:47:02,520
We will cut the head that doesn't obey
Mongols.

876
01:47:30,170 --> 01:47:35,070
How am I going to get out of this
situation, my Allah?

877
01:47:43,380 --> 01:47:46,870
Give me power to destroy my enemy

878
01:47:48,820 --> 01:47:51,200
Help my brothers.

879
01:48:13,950 --> 01:48:16,490
I wonder what you are up to, Sıddık.

880
01:48:18,950 --> 01:48:21,970
I told you you'd go through a challenging
task.

881
01:48:22,050 --> 01:48:23,740
Are you ready?

882
01:48:24,390 --> 01:48:27,510
What do you order, Osman Bey?
Command me.

883
01:48:28,820 --> 01:48:31,730
You are going to betray me.

884
01:48:36,360 --> 01:48:41,250
Help me, my Allah.
Help me.

885
01:48:43,280 --> 01:48:45,490
Help me, my Allah.

886
01:49:30,700 --> 01:49:33,290
You have been following me.

887
01:49:33,520 --> 01:49:36,960
Did you think that I wouldn't notice you?
Who are you?

888
01:49:37,610 --> 01:49:39,870
You'll find out, Osman Bey.

889
01:49:51,870 --> 01:49:56,950
Today, the fortified crescent will
brighten up, Osman Bey.

890
01:49:58,490 --> 01:50:00,850
Your time has come.

891
01:50:26,220 --> 01:50:28,150
Dündar.

892
01:50:28,810 --> 01:50:31,080
Ah Dündar.

893
01:50:31,820 --> 01:50:36,820
Dündar, who keeps silent while his
Alps are being tortured.

894
01:50:38,700 --> 01:50:42,000
You ruined my Ertuğrul Bey's entrustment.

895
01:50:47,370 --> 01:50:53,110
No, no. Bamsı Bey can't keep silent
to this cruelty.

896
01:50:54,650 --> 01:50:57,760
What are you doing Bamsı Bey?
They are looking for you everywhere.

897
01:50:57,980 --> 01:51:01,820
I prefer dying to keep silent,
Selcan Hatun.

898
01:51:02,610 --> 01:51:07,560
We are not dead yet, thanks to Allah.
Follow me.

899
01:51:25,250 --> 01:51:26,840
Bala.

900
01:51:48,690 --> 01:51:50,790
Gonca Hatun.

901
01:51:51,900 --> 01:51:54,790
Bala Hatun, is it ready?

902
01:51:56,180 --> 01:52:00,000
Osman Bey didn't leave his alps to
Balgay's hand, Bamsı Bey.

903
01:52:02,460 --> 01:52:08,250
My Ertuğrul Bey's entrustment is in
good hands, Bamsı Bey. We won't give up.

904
01:53:33,430 --> 01:53:38,020
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.
(in the name of Allah, the merciful and compassionate)

905
01:55:01,620 --> 01:55:03,500
Who are you?

906
01:55:15,830 --> 01:55:17,800
What do you want from me?

907
01:55:17,800 --> 01:55:21,640
We don't have the answers, Osman Bey.
You'll get the answers inside.

908
01:55:29,760 --> 01:55:31,760
Enter if you are ready.

909
01:56:43,640 --> 01:56:47,570
Is this dog responsible for these?

910
01:56:51,440 --> 01:56:53,460
Let go of my brother, you ignoble!

911
01:56:58,480 --> 01:57:01,010
Stand back, fool, stand back so that...

912
01:57:01,010 --> 01:57:03,980
you don't die under my feet like
a bug.

913
01:57:15,480 --> 01:57:20,040
I'll make you regret, Balgay.

914
01:57:23,420 --> 01:57:29,500
You'll be drowned of the blood you shed
because of your cruelty.

915
01:57:44,530 --> 01:57:49,150
Seeing your outfit, you are a hatun of
tradition.

916
01:57:49,150 --> 01:57:53,920
But, it is obvious that you don't know me.

917
01:57:56,010 --> 01:58:00,500
They call me Mongol's iron-fist Bangal!

918
01:58:00,500 --> 01:58:04,360
I'll make lakes out of blood,
mountains out of bones!

919
01:58:04,400 --> 01:58:08,810
The fire rises where I go!

920
01:58:09,750 --> 01:58:17,420
This glorious tent has been a grave to the
cruel, Balgay.

921
01:58:18,390 --> 01:58:21,530
You will be one of them too.

922
01:58:23,940 --> 01:58:28,240
Your greed wakens my anger.

923
01:58:29,750 --> 01:58:32,020
Blue-eyed son.

924
01:58:40,910 --> 01:58:46,240
As a warning to others, I will...

925
01:58:50,100 --> 01:58:52,040
I will...

926
01:58:53,780 --> 01:58:57,300
Kill you slowly.

927
01:59:38,670 --> 01:59:41,290
Help us, my Allah.

928
01:59:43,110 --> 01:59:46,850
Fame Kayı Bey Sergeant Samsa.

929
01:59:46,860 --> 01:59:48,240
Hosshht!

930
01:59:54,970 --> 01:59:57,400
You'll die like a dog.

931
02:00:17,830 --> 02:00:21,050
Ertugrul's famous servant.

932
02:00:21,050 --> 02:00:22,580
Don't.

933
02:00:23,970 --> 02:00:26,600
Abdurrahman Ghazi.

934
02:00:32,510 --> 02:00:34,340
Ignoble dog!

935
02:00:37,870 --> 02:00:39,690
Don't.

936
02:00:44,940 --> 02:00:51,660
You will all watch what happens to those
who don't obey Mongols.

937
02:01:01,940 --> 02:01:04,690
- No, no no!
- Wait!

938
02:01:05,490 --> 02:01:06,900
Let him go.

939
02:01:11,980 --> 02:01:13,880
Leave my son alone.

940
02:01:15,320 --> 02:01:16,640
Leave him alone.

941
02:01:21,580 --> 02:01:24,080
Leave my son alone.

942
02:01:26,840 --> 02:01:32,310
Your hatuns are courageous as well as
your men.

943
02:01:33,470 --> 02:01:38,020
Balgay likes courageous men and women.

944
02:01:49,860 --> 02:01:55,060
Are those women diligent as well as
being courageous?

945
02:01:55,260 --> 02:01:57,210
Let's see.

946
02:02:05,130 --> 02:02:08,760
Bring me food and Kumis(drink).

947
02:02:08,850 --> 02:02:13,750
I prefer dying to serve you.

948
02:02:16,400 --> 02:02:23,990
Then, watch me drinking this son's blood
instead of Kumis.

949
02:02:28,170 --> 02:02:29,780
No.

950
02:02:30,050 --> 02:02:31,660
No!
No!

951
02:02:31,800 --> 02:02:33,140
Wait!

952
02:02:40,640 --> 02:02:42,410
I'll bring.

953
02:02:47,280 --> 02:02:52,010
Cut me meat.
Don't linger!

954
02:02:52,730 --> 02:02:57,290
Aunt.
Don't.

955
02:03:04,500 --> 02:03:06,800
Aunt, don't!

956
02:04:11,520 --> 02:04:14,240
You'll die, Balgay!

957
02:04:52,280 --> 02:04:54,250
Who are you?

958
02:04:54,950 --> 02:05:00,920
We are the Almighty Sycamore's Turks,
Osman Bey.

959
02:05:04,830 --> 02:05:11,760
We got in flames in Ergenekon, and
We burnt the whole world in Malazgirt.

960
02:05:12,780 --> 02:05:19,590
And now we came here to open a way
from Ötüken to Söğütlü.

961
02:05:20,330 --> 02:05:24,750
I haven't heard of you until now.

962
02:05:26,080 --> 02:05:30,670
We show up in the most difficult times.

963
02:05:30,830 --> 02:05:36,640
We came to brighten up your way with
our ancestor Oguz's light.

964
02:06:13,310 --> 02:06:15,510
My father's dagger.

965
02:06:26,840 --> 02:06:28,930
Masha Allah (praise be!)

966
02:06:37,430 --> 02:06:42,400
Both of your father Ertuğrul Gazi and your
grandfather Süleyman Shah...

967
02:06:42,690 --> 02:06:45,150
was in our society, son.

968
02:06:46,480 --> 02:06:53,540
Now, our crescents point at you.

969
02:07:40,020 --> 02:07:47,420
Turks' latest state Seljuq Empire has
been destroyed by Mongols.

970
02:07:47,860 --> 02:07:52,020
However, hopelessness is not in tradition.

971
02:07:53,740 --> 02:07:57,150
In this country, where we have come thanks
to our tradition...

972
02:07:58,190 --> 02:08:00,510
the situation is bad.

973
02:08:02,040 --> 02:08:04,300
We don't serve to servants.

974
02:08:04,630 --> 02:08:06,690
We obey no one.

975
02:08:07,140 --> 02:08:09,030
However...

976
02:08:09,250 --> 02:08:11,790
The cruelty is all around us.

977
02:08:17,320 --> 02:08:20,090
Our people are about to be out of hope.

978
02:08:20,360 --> 02:08:25,540
Contrarily, the Turk's hope is the
country, son.

979
02:08:29,250 --> 02:08:36,200
This hope sent your father Ertuğrul Gazi
to this country.

980
02:08:37,710 --> 02:08:48,390
Until the sky falls, until the ground
cracks, every Turk is a state.

981
02:08:49,780 --> 02:08:54,550
So, even if a city falls,
the tradition stands still.

982
02:08:55,270 --> 02:08:59,520
Eyvallah, Eyvallah (thanks) but...

983
02:08:59,920 --> 02:09:02,270
Balgay conquered everywhere.

984
02:09:03,290 --> 02:09:07,910
Mongols celebrate the victory in
Turk tribes!

985
02:09:08,440 --> 02:09:11,080
We are here for this.

986
02:09:11,080 --> 02:09:16,110
Bury your sorrow to the hope.

987
02:09:16,830 --> 02:09:20,170
And, remember, Osman Bey.

988
02:09:20,590 --> 02:09:29,510
There can't be Turks without azan,
freedom, and a state!

989
02:09:48,230 --> 02:09:53,860
The power that will stop Balgay is in this
chest.

990
02:11:00,820 --> 02:11:03,550
Balgay liked you.

991
02:12:12,950 --> 02:12:14,820
Drink.

992
02:12:22,000 --> 02:12:23,870
Drink.

993
02:12:39,990 --> 02:12:41,370
Drink.

994
02:12:42,000 --> 02:12:43,270
Drink.

995
02:12:44,340 --> 02:12:47,360
Or I'll make you drink that son's blood.

996
02:12:47,570 --> 02:12:49,350
- No!
- No!

997
02:13:17,210 --> 02:13:21,260
Hey, my Allah, who is the owner
of the ground and sky.

998
02:13:24,830 --> 02:13:29,310
This community, this state is yours.

999
02:13:32,840 --> 02:13:35,770
May we don't bow to the cruels.

1000
02:13:35,820 --> 02:13:39,710
May fear don't capture our hearts,
my Allah.

1001
02:13:44,010 --> 02:13:48,620
Give me power to resurrect this state!

1002
02:13:54,680 --> 02:13:59,080
Make Turks rule this age!

1003
02:13:59,360 --> 02:14:04,000
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com